---
/**
 * How to use tony, for someone who has just finished signing in.
 *
 * Written for the agent-native flow, which is the only one the setup walks
 * anyone into: install, sign in, then tell an agent. The API-key path still
 * exists and is deliberately not documented here — it is the headless entry
 * point, not the thing to teach first.
 */
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
---

<Shell title="How to use tony" description="Set tony up once, then ask your agent to review a branch.">
  <div class="hero">
    <p class="cap">Documentation</p>
    <h1>Set it up once. Then just ask.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      tony doesn't call a model. Your coding agent writes the review, and tony turns it
      into a page you can share.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">Setup</p>
    <h2 class="big">Three steps, once per machine.</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Install</h3>
          <div class="cmd">
            <code><span class="p">$</span> curl -fsSL https://tony-cli.com/install.sh | sh</code>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Connect it to your agent</h3>
          <p>Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Amp and Codex. <b>Restart your agent after.</b></p>
          <div class="cmd">
            <code><span class="p">$</span> tony connect</code>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Sign in</h3>
          <p>Opens your browser. It tells you when you're done.</p>
          <div class="cmd">
            <code><span class="p">$</span> tony login</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            In a cloud sandbox, like Amp or Codex cloud, skip this. Your agent shows you a link
            to approve instead.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">Using it</p>
    <h2 class="big">Ask your agent.</h2>
    <div class="cmd">
      <code><span class="p">&gt;</span> review this branch with tony</code>
    </div>
    <p class="body" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
      Or name a range: <code>review main...HEAD with tony</code>. You get a link back.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">What comes back</p>
    <h2 class="big">A page, not a chat message.</h2>
    <div class="three">
      <div>
        <span class="n">01</span>
        <h3>Every change explained</h3>
        <p>What it does now, what it did before, and why it matters.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="n">02</span>
        <h3>Blast radius</h3>
        <p>Code outside the diff that the change affects.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="n">03</span>
        <h3>How it works</h3>
        <p>Each flow the change touches, step by step, before and after.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">Commands</p>
    <h2 class="big">The rest.</h2>
    <dl class="cmds">
      <dt>tony connect [claude|cursor|amp|codex]</dt>
      <dd>Connect one agent instead of all of them.</dd>
      <dt>tony logout</dt>
      <dd>Sign this machine out.</dd>
      <dt>tony update</dt>
      <dd>Update tony.</dd>
      <dt>tony uninstall</dt>
      <dd>Remove tony and everything it saved.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" style="border-bottom:0">
    <p class="cap">Trouble</p>
    <h2 class="big">Your agent can't find tony?</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Quit it fully and reopen it. Agents only load their tools at startup. Still nothing?
      Run <code>tony connect</code> again.
    </p>
  </section>
</Shell>
